-- Aroma lexicon v2 (data only): the lexicon review, with the owner's own calls.
--
-- Owner, 2026-09-29: review the aroma list against what sommeliers and wine
-- writers actually say, "still in the WSET spirit however, nothing too
-- unscientific", plus three decisions of their own: "just having apple is too
-- vague. Green apple / red apple distinction is needed"; "i dont think dried or
-- cooked fruit should be in primary aromas"; "missing smoked meat and olives
-- note". Approved as one change set, with "Keep jammy", "Black and green olive"
-- and the two saved notes' "dried fruit" becoming "raisin".
--
-- Lexicon (144 -> 150 terms, 69/25/50 -> 73/24/53 by origin, still 18 groups):
--   renamed in place (same ids, so every note and typical-wine link follows):
--     apple -> green apple (Green fruit); toast -> toasted bread (Yeast only:
--     Oak and White wine toast stay); flint -> flint / struck match; saltiness
--     -> saline;
--   added: red apple, lime zest, pomegranate, black olive, green olive,
--     ginger (PRIMARY Spice; the TERTIARY White wine ginger stays), smoked
--     meat, truffle (Red wine and White wine), black tea, beeswax;
--   removed: dried fruit and cooked fruit (out of PRIMARY Fruit ripeness,
--     which keeps unripe fruit, ripe fruit and jammy), kerosene (petrol covers
--     it), graham cracker (biscuit covers it), cooked red plum (cooked plum).
-- Saved notes: two notes held dried fruit and one of them cooked red plum;
--   they become raisin (TERTIARY Red wine) and cooked plum, keeping their
--   nose/palate flags.
-- Typical wines: the 42 approved typical-wine changes (red apple where the
--   wine is riper than green apple, smoked meat and black olive in the
--   northern Rhône, truffle, black tea, ginger, lime zest, beeswax, the
--   dried-fruit rows remapped), Rioja Gran Reserva's cooked red plum ->
--   cooked plum, Tawny Port's orange peel dropped (Citrus fruit shows for
--   white wines only, so no taster could pick it on a red) and "dried fruit"
--   dropped from Oloroso's description. 1100 -> 1125 typical-wine aroma rows.
--
-- New terms follow the lexicon's placement rule (20260902210000): each lands
-- right after its anchor (found by origin, group and term, since mushroom,
-- cinnamon and others repeat across groups) and everything above shifts up by
-- one; the removed terms leave gaps. sort_order ends 1..156, unique.
-- Order: renames, new terms, saved notes, typical wines, then the removals,
-- each only once nothing references it (wine_archetype_aromas cascades, so a
-- stray link would vanish silently; wset_note_aromas would refuse the delete).
--
-- Written against the live state of 2026-09-29: every value this relies on is
-- asserted first and the result asserted after, in the same transaction.
-- Spec, votes and sources: data/training/aroma-lexicon-v2-2026-09-29.json.
-- No begin/commit: the applier owns the transaction.

set local lock_timeout = '10s';

-- Pre-state.
do $pre$
begin
  if not ((select count(*) from wset_aroma_terms) = 144) then raise exception 'pre-state: expected 144 aroma terms'; end if;
  if not ((select count(*) from wset_aroma_terms where origin = 'PRIMARY') = 69 and (select count(*) from wset_aroma_terms where origin = 'SECONDARY') = 25 and (select count(*) from wset_aroma_terms where origin = 'TERTIARY') = 50) then raise exception 'pre-state: origin split is not 69/25/50'; end if;
  if not ((select count(distinct group_name) from wset_aroma_terms) = 18) then raise exception 'pre-state: expected 18 groups'; end if;
  if not ((select count(distinct sort_order) from wset_aroma_terms) = 144 and (select max(sort_order) from wset_aroma_terms) = 145) then raise exception 'pre-state: sort_order is not unique 1..145'; end if;
  if not ((select count(*) from wine_archetype_aromas) = 1100) then raise exception 'pre-state: expected 1100 typical-wine aroma rows'; end if;
  if not ((select count(*) from wine_archetype_aromas where kind = 'NOSE') = 574 and (select count(*) from wine_archetype_aromas where kind = 'PALATE') = 526 and (select count(*) from wine_archetype_aromas where signature) = 149) then raise exception 'pre-state: typical-wine aroma split is not 574 NOSE / 526 PALATE / 149 signature'; end if;
  if not ((select count(*) from wset_note_aromas) = 113) then raise exception 'pre-state: expected 113 saved-note aroma rows'; end if;
